  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1212 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nStrong high pressure at the surface and aloft remains locked in\nhere this week, pumping up the heat and humidity in the process.\nOur prolonged duration Heat Advisory running the course of the\nweek looks to survive with ease, with all sites reaching into\nthe triple digits daily. Pushing past 105 degrees will be more\nhit and miss, and tops the whole week looks to be near but not\nin excess of 110 degrees, at least by means of the current data.\nWednesday-Thursday play the hottest, with most sites settling\nsomewhere from 103-106 degrees, though there may be sporadic \nlocal exceptions slightly higher or lower.\n\nLonger-range modeling still brings a chance of pcpn in toward\nthe week's end, namely Friday-Saturday; but the chance is small,\nsmaller than it was yesterday, and as such, if the trend\ncontinues, it's possible the headline gets lengthened into\nSaturday. We won't jump on that this early, but it bears\nwatching as the week goes on.",
